WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.491 --> 00:00:03.324
(classical music)

00:00:06.787 --> 00:00:07.697
- Babe.

00:00:07.697 --> 00:00:09.238
- Huh? Yeah?

00:00:09.238 --> 00:00:11.147
- What are you thinking?

00:00:11.147 --> 00:00:14.538
- (laughs) Nothin' really.

00:00:14.538 --> 00:00:16.215
- You are not thinking nothing.

00:00:16.215 --> 00:00:18.312
- (laughs) Yes, I am, I.
- No, you're not.

00:00:18.312 --> 00:00:19.796
You are a thoughtful person.
- Yeah.

00:00:19.796 --> 00:00:21.073
- There's no way that you are thinking.

00:00:21.073 --> 00:00:22.331
I am never just not thinking

00:00:22.331 --> 00:00:23.572
absolutely nothing.
- Right.

00:00:23.572 --> 00:00:24.504
Right.
- That doesn't work like that.

00:00:24.504 --> 00:00:25.494
- You definitely don't.

00:00:25.494 --> 00:00:26.626
I do though, I swear.

00:00:26.626 --> 00:00:27.839
I have an analogy for this.

00:00:27.839 --> 00:00:29.434
Go with me on this, just
walk with me on this.

00:00:29.434 --> 00:00:30.267
Come here.

00:00:30.267 --> 00:00:31.136
- Like, literally walk with you?

00:00:31.136 --> 00:00:31.969
- Yeah, like literally
walk with me on this.

00:00:31.969 --> 00:00:32.802
- Okay.
- Come on.

00:00:32.802 --> 00:00:33.678
(light chimes ringing)

00:00:33.678 --> 00:00:34.655
Walk with me, come here.

00:00:34.655 --> 00:00:36.660
(classical music)

00:00:36.660 --> 00:00:37.887
Alright, so the way I see it.

00:00:37.887 --> 00:00:38.720
- Mmm.

00:00:38.720 --> 00:00:40.673
- We organize our thoughts
differently from one another.

00:00:40.673 --> 00:00:42.634
Your brain is kind of like this spaghetti.

00:00:42.634 --> 00:00:44.381
And your thoughts are like this sauce.

00:00:44.381 --> 00:00:46.264
My brain is kind of like this waffle.

00:00:46.264 --> 00:00:47.732
And my thoughts are like this syrup.

00:00:47.732 --> 00:00:50.209
Now if you'll notice,
this syrup and this sauce

00:00:50.209 --> 00:00:51.293
are the exact same amount.

00:00:51.293 --> 00:00:52.272
- Okay.

00:00:52.272 --> 00:00:53.858
- Your thoughts cover your brain

00:00:53.858 --> 00:00:55.853
like tomato sauce covers
spaghetti noodles.

00:00:55.853 --> 00:00:58.806
When I pick your brain, you're
always covered in thoughts.

00:00:58.806 --> 00:01:01.513
- Me on the other hand,
my brain is like a waffle.

00:01:01.513 --> 00:01:05.195
My thoughts cover my brain
like syrup on waffle squares.

00:01:05.195 --> 00:01:06.028
Ya' know what I mean?

00:01:06.028 --> 00:01:06.861
- Yeah.

00:01:06.861 --> 00:01:08.718
- Right, well some waffle
squares will have syrup.

00:01:08.718 --> 00:01:10.842
But some squares'll be totally empty.

00:01:10.842 --> 00:01:13.343
So sometimes when you ask
me, like what am I thinking,

00:01:13.343 --> 00:01:15.044
baby, you just got an empty waffle square.

00:01:15.044 --> 00:01:16.785
Like I'm not saying I'm dumb,

00:01:16.785 --> 00:01:17.898
I'm not saying I don't have thoughts,

00:01:17.898 --> 00:01:18.734
I have lots of thoughts.

00:01:18.734 --> 00:01:22.783
I just compartmentalize and
maybe have one thing at a time.

00:01:22.783 --> 00:01:25.164
- This is almost insightful.

00:01:25.164 --> 00:01:26.843
- (laughs)

00:01:26.843 --> 00:01:27.918
- This is kind of insightful.

00:01:27.918 --> 00:01:28.849
- It's a little bit insightful.

00:01:28.849 --> 00:01:30.191
- Okay.

00:01:30.191 --> 00:01:31.657
- I feel like it makes a
lot more sense to you now

00:01:31.657 --> 00:01:33.307
and you're not gonna me
so much when you ask me,

00:01:33.307 --> 00:01:34.140
do you have thoughts?

00:01:34.140 --> 00:01:35.500
And I'm like, no.

00:01:35.500 --> 00:01:38.333
(classical music)

